      "evidence_box_px": [
        988,
        398,
        1631,
        652
      ],
      "print_plain": "From the barline at x 988 to the end of the system-2 staves at x 1631 is the first part of one cadenza. The stroke at x 1146 is the stems of the fermata chord, not a barline: the gap between the staves there is blank. No closing barline is printed, and the same bar continues on system 3. The longest voice is the upper staff. It begins with an open half note tied to an open half note under a fermata (2 + 2 quarters). A second voice of two filled quarter-note heads under those halves totals 2 quarters. The upper voice then continues with an eighth rest (1/2), two eighth-note triplets (1 + 1), a dotted quarter (3/2), two eighths (1/2 + 1/2), a quarter-note chord with a fermata (1), an eighth rest (1/2), and four sixteenths (1). That continuation is 15/2 quarters. The longest voice is 4 + 15/2 = 23/2 quarters. The lower staff has the fermata chord, then an eighth rest with a fermata and a half rest with a fermata, and is shorter."
    },
    {
      "physical_bar": 13,
      "id": "P013",
      "capacity_q": "17/2",
      "capacity_plain": "17/2 quarters, the longest voice",
      "kind": "system-3 part of the same cadenza bar, closed by a thin-thick double bar",
      "flags": [
        "CADENZA",
        "SPLIT_REGION",
        "PARTIAL",
        "DOUBLE_BARLINE",
        "SECTION_BOUNDARY"
      ],
      "page": 1,
      "system": 3,
      "crop_path": "source_crops/system_03.png",
      "onset_q": "0",
      "evidence_space": "page_px",
      "evidence_box_px": [
        240,
        676,
        780,
        980
      ],
      "print_plain": "System 3 opens with a brace and the reprinted clefs. No barline stands before the notes. This is the second part of the cadenza that began at x 988 on system 2, and it ends at the thin-thick double bar. The longest voice is the upper staff: an eighth rest (1/2) outside the following triplet, one eighth-note triplet of three beamed eighths under a single 3 (1), a dotted quarter (3/2), one flagged eighth with no triplet numeral (1/2), two further eighth-note triplets (1 + 1), and six ordinary eighths in two beamed groups of three with no triplet numeral (3), ending at the thin stroke. Those durations sum to 17/2 quarters. A lower voice, a dotted half then a chord with a turn and a fermata, sounds under the first part of that line and is shorter. The lower staff is empty until the double bar. The thin stroke is at x 763 and the thick stroke at x 767-768, with no repeat dots."
    }
